Description: TEMP_FAILURE_RETRY is a glibc macro musl doesn't have: the sandbox's process_util.h defines it.
Forwarded: not-needed (Alpine's musl patch; Alpine carries it)
Origin: Alpine Linux aports ecc3ce96955f459cf819602db39593b42ded8515, community/chromium/temp-failure-retry.patch
Rebased to apply exactly (Jam OS's applier takes no fuzz): the body below is the same change made again by diff -u against this tarball.

random glibc macro, not provided by musl.
https://www.gnu.org/software/libc/manual/html_node/Interrupted-Primitives.html

--- a/sandbox/linux/suid/process_util.h
+++ b/sandbox/linux/suid/process_util.h
@@ -12,6 +12,14 @@
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
 
+// Some additional functions
+# define TEMP_FAILURE_RETRY(expression) \
+	(__extension__			\
+	 ({ long int __result;		\
+	  do __result = (long int) (expression); \
+	  while (__result == -1L && errno == EINTR); \
+	  __result; }))
+
 // This adjusts /proc/process/oom_score_adj so the Linux OOM killer
 // will prefer certain process types over others. The range for the
 // adjustment is [-1000, 1000], with [0, 1000] being user accessible.
